{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>You — and you shall be bowed down.</b> [וישחך] is a noun, like וישעך תתן לנו. The meaning: the opposite of your pride." "<b>תסג</b> — your wife. The samekh is like shin: she will reach pregnancy but not give birth. All this is because of the violence you have done, each man to his fellow, the rich man to the poor man."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra cites Micah 6:14; the comparison word וישעך appears in Psalm 60:7 or similar; rendered as quoted.", 1 "Ibn Ezra reads תסג as a form applied to 'your wife'; he parses samekh as equivalent to shin in the root."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:14:11.441765673Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}